Math fpu User Documentation Ver1.0 :
------------------------------------

Summary :
---------
	1>Installation
	2>Requirements
	3>Usage
	4>WARNINGS!!!!.
	5>Updates...
	6>Instructions

------------------------------------------------------

	1>Installation :
	----------------

  That amiga library is easy to install.
You only need to coyp mathfpu.library inside your
LIBS: drawer.

  That original archive can be copied and distributed 
if it is not modified in any way.

------------------------------------------------------

	2>Requirements :
	----------------

  This library can only be used on amiga equipped with:
	- 68881 or 68882 math co-pro
				or
	- 68040 or 68060 cpu ( with fpu )

If you use that library when there is only a 68000,
68020 or 68030 processor,It will crash your system.

------------------------------------------------------

	3>Usage :
	---------

  This library was made to allow you the use of math()
instruction set on 68881/2,68040 and 68060 processors.
It use direct fpu instructions and conversion to gain
maximal speed.You can use it like all others amiga
libraries.

------------------------------------------------------

	4>WARNINGS!!! :
	---------------

  - The author of this library is not and can not be
responsible for any damages caused by the use of that
library.You use it at your own risk.

  - This library must not be used on amiga which are
not equipped with 68881,68882,68040(+fpu) or 68060(fpu)
processors or your system should crash !!!

  - This library has been tested on A1200+68060+32Mram

